        <p class="mb-8 rounded-md border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-gray-900"><strong>Takes effect January 1, 2027.</strong> This is version 1.3 of the Marketplace Transaction Terms. Until then, version 1.2 remains in effect: <a href="/legal/transaction-terms" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,45%)] underline">read version 1.2</a>.</p>

        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900">Marketplace Transaction Terms</h1>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Effective Date:</strong> January 1, 2027 <strong>Version:</strong> 1.3</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">1. Scope and Applicability</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">These Marketplace Transaction Terms ("Transaction Terms") govern all transactions initiated, facilitated, or conducted through the BreederHQ Marketplace, including but not limited to animal purchases, breeding service bookings, Service Provider bookings, waitlist reservation fees, and stud service fees. These Transaction Terms supplement and are incorporated into the BreederHQ Terms of Service.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Subject to §12, by participating in any transaction through the Marketplace, whether as a Provider (Breeder/Seller Provider or Service Provider) or Buyer, you agree to be bound by these Transaction Terms in addition to the general Terms of Service, the Acceptable Use Policy, the Legal Definitions Schedule, and the applicable Provider Agreement or Buyer Terms. The Privacy Policy describes how BreederHQ handles personal information; it is a notice, not one of these agreements (Terms of Service §11).</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Capitalized terms used in these Transaction Terms have the meanings given in the BreederHQ Legal Definitions Schedule, which is incorporated into these Transaction Terms by reference.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">2. Platform Role in Transactions</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.1 Introduction Venue; Not a Party</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ acts solely as a technology platform that connects Providers and Buyers. <strong>BreederHQ is NOT a party to any transaction between Providers and Buyers.</strong> All transactions are direct agreements between the Provider and the Buyer.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>BreederHQ introduces Buyers to Providers; it is not a party to what they agree.</strong> BreederHQ does not negotiate, set, approve, guarantee, or enforce the price, terms, conditions, warranties, health guarantees, deposits, reservation fees, refunds, delivery, or outcome of any agreement between a Provider and a Buyer. The Provider and the Buyer own their transaction and every dispute about it. A listing, storefront, message, waitlist, booking, invoice, payment request, or other feature of the Services that displays or records a term a Provider or Buyer has set does not make that term BreederHQ's.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.2 Payment Processing</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Payments arising from Marketplace transactions are processed by a third-party payment processor. Depending on the transaction type and the Provider's payment configuration, a payment may be processed directly on the Provider's connected payment account, or BreederHQ may provide payment-related platform or settlement services in connection with it.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>BreederHQ does not act as an escrow agent, does not hold funds as a fiduciary or in trust for any User, and does not retain Provider transaction proceeds as its own property, except to recover amounts a Provider owes under §6.4.</strong> Where funds are routed through BreederHQ's payment infrastructure, they are held solely in connection with settlement, and BreederHQ acquires no beneficial interest in them. BreederHQ acts as the Provider's limited payments agent for that purpose, as set out in §2.7 of the Terms of Service.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ does not set prices, does not determine refund policy, and does not control whether a Provider fulfills a transaction. All payment disputes, chargebacks, and refund processing are subject to the payment processor's terms of service in addition to these Transaction Terms.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>BreederHQ's own role in payments.</strong> BreederHQ's role in payments is limited to the following: (a) charging Providers, through the payment processor, for BreederHQ's own subscriptions and fees, for which BreederHQ is the seller; (b) supplying software through which Providers request, accept, record, and refund payments from Buyers, which are made to the Provider and processed by the payment processor; and (c) where a payment is routed through BreederHQ's payment infrastructure, acting as the Provider's limited payments agent as described above. In none of these roles does BreederHQ decide whether a payment, deposit, reservation fee, or refund is owed between a Provider and a Buyer, or become a party to their transaction.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.3 No Guarantees</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ does not guarantee:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>The quality, health, genetics, temperament, or condition of any animal;</li><li>The accuracy of any listing, description, photo, or health record;</li><li>The completion or outcome of any transaction;</li><li>The identity, credentials, qualifications, or licensure of any Provider (other than displaying the passthrough described in §2.6 of the Terms of Service, which is not BreederHQ's warranty);</li><li>The financial ability or intent of any Buyer to complete a transaction;</li><li>The authenticity, currency, or accuracy of any document a Provider uploads in connection with a Credential Attestation, professional license, registry record, or other representation;</li><li>The continued validity of any credential, license, certification, or accreditation a Provider has attested to or for which a Provider has uploaded supporting documentation;</li><li>The accuracy of any "Confirmed via [Registry] registry" indicator after the timestamp shown on the indicator at the time of display;</li><li>The quality, safety, professional competence, or outcome of any service rendered by a Service Provider.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.4 Contract Tools</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ's contract templates, editing tools, AI-assisted conversion, and electronic signing are tools that BreederHQ supplies. The Provider and the Buyer choose and own the contents of any Transaction Contract between them. A template, including a template BreederHQ provides, is a starting point; it is not legal advice, not a recommendation that any term suits a transaction, and not a term of BreederHQ's. BreederHQ does not become a party to a Transaction Contract by supplying the tools used to prepare, sign, store, or display it. §7C of the Terms of Service governs these tools.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">3. Waitlist Reservation Fees</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.1 Nature of Reservation Fees</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A waitlist reservation fee is a payment made by a Buyer to a Provider to reserve a position on a Provider's waitlist for a future animal or litter. Reservation fees are agreements between the Buyer and the Provider.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.2 Reservation Fee Refund Policy</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Reservation fee refund policies are set by each individual Provider and should be clearly stated in the Provider's listing or waitlist terms. <strong>BreederHQ does not set, enforce, or adjudicate reservation fee refund policies.</strong> Buyers are responsible for reviewing and understanding the Provider's refund policy before paying a reservation fee.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.3 Provider Obligations Regarding Reservation Fees</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Providers who accept waitlist reservation fees agree to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Clearly disclose their reservation fee amount and refund policy before accepting payment;</li><li>Honor the refund policy as stated at the time the reservation fee was accepted;</li><li>Communicate promptly with Buyers regarding waitlist status, expected timelines, and any changes;</li><li>Refund reservation fees in accordance with their stated policy if they are unable to fulfill the reservation.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.4 Buyer Acknowledgments Regarding Reservation Fees</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">By paying a waitlist reservation fee, Buyers acknowledge that:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>The reservation fee is owed and payable to the Provider. BreederHQ does not acquire an ownership interest in the reservation fee merely by providing Marketplace or payment-related services, and any platform fee BreederHQ charges is separate from the reservation fee;</li><li>Refund terms are determined by the Provider, not BreederHQ;</li><li>There is no guarantee of receiving a specific animal, and availability depends on litter outcomes and Provider selection processes;</li><li>BreederHQ has no ability to force a Provider to issue a refund.</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">4. Animal Purchases</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.1 Listing Accuracy</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Providers are solely responsible for the accuracy of all listing information, including but not limited to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Species, breed, age, sex, and registration status;</li><li>Health testing results, vaccinations, and veterinary records;</li><li>Pedigree information and genetic data;</li><li>Photos and descriptions;</li><li>Pricing and availability.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.2 Health and Condition</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">All representations regarding an animal's health, genetics, and condition are made solely by the Provider. Buyers are strongly encouraged to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Request independent veterinary examination before completing a purchase;</li><li>Verify registration and pedigree claims through the relevant breed registry;</li><li>Obtain written health guarantees directly from the Provider;</li><li>Inspect the animal in person or via live video before purchase when possible.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.3 Transfer of Ownership</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The transfer of ownership, including registration paperwork, health records, and physical delivery of the animal, is the sole responsibility of the Provider and Buyer. BreederHQ does not facilitate, verify, or guarantee the transfer process.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.4 Transportation and Delivery</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Arrangements for transportation and delivery of animals are made directly between the Provider and Buyer. BreederHQ assumes no responsibility for:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Shipping or transportation logistics;</li><li>The condition of the animal during or after transport;</li><li>Compliance with state, federal, or international animal transport regulations;</li><li>Health certificates, import/export permits, or other required documentation.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.5 Animals and Meeting in Person</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Buying, receiving, handling, transporting, and caring for an animal, booking services for one, and meeting another User in person or visiting their premises, carry inherent risks, including bites and other injury, disease, property damage, and loss. BreederHQ does not screen, vet, or supervise Users, does not arrange or attend meetings, visits, pickups, or deliveries, and does not control any animal or premises. Take sensible precautions, such as meeting in a safe place and having an animal examined by your own veterinarian. To the fullest extent permitted by law, you assume those risks as between you and BreederHQ. This Section does not limit BreederHQ's liability for its own fraud, willful misconduct, or gross negligence, or for death or personal injury caused by its own negligence, or any right or remedy that cannot lawfully be waived. The sentence in this Section by which you assume those risks does not apply to a Consumer, as defined in §10.2(d) of the Terms of Service, who lives in New Jersey.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">5. Breeding Service Bookings and Service Provider Bookings</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.1 Scope</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Breeding service bookings include but are not limited to stud services, artificial insemination services, semen sales, and embryo transfers listed on the Marketplace. Service Provider bookings include but are not limited to farrier, training, veterinary, grooming, transport, and pet-sitting services listed on the Marketplace.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.2 Service Terms</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The specific terms of any breeding service or Service Provider booking—including pricing, scheduling, methods, qualifications, scope, return breeding guarantees, cancellation policies, and outcome expectations—are negotiated and agreed upon directly between the Provider and Buyer. BreederHQ does not set or enforce service terms.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.3 Outcome Disclaimer</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ makes no representations or warranties regarding the outcome of any breeding service or Service Provider booking, including but not limited to conception rates, litter size, offspring health, genetic outcomes, animal response to training, treatment outcomes, or any other result of professional services rendered by a Provider.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">6. Refunds, Returns, and Cancellations</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">6.1 Provider-Set Policies</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Each Provider is responsible for establishing and communicating their own refund, return, and cancellation policies. These policies must be disclosed to Buyers before a transaction is completed.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">6.2 BreederHQ's Role in Refunds</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ does not determine whether a refund is owed and does not guarantee any refund. A Provider remains responsible for authorizing any refund due under its policy or applicable law. If a refund is owed:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>The Provider is responsible for funding and directing any refund owed, issued through the original payment method where feasible or as otherwise agreed with the Buyer;</li><li>BreederHQ may, at its sole discretion, assist in facilitating communication between the parties but has no obligation to do so;</li><li>BreederHQ platform fees (if applicable) are non-refundable unless otherwise stated.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">6.3 Chargebacks</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">If a Buyer initiates a chargeback through their payment provider:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>The chargeback is processed by our third-party payment processor in accordance with their dispute resolution procedures;</li><li>The Provider is responsible for responding to chargeback claims and providing evidence as required;</li><li>Excessive chargebacks against a Provider's account may result in suspension or termination of the Provider's Marketplace access.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">6.4 Platform Chargeback Recovery</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Where a Marketplace transaction is routed through BreederHQ's payment infrastructure on behalf of the Provider, or where the payment processor holds BreederHQ responsible for losses on the Provider's connected payment account, chargebacks, reversals, payment disputes, or negative balances resulting from a Provider's transaction may cause a debit to, or other financial loss in, BreederHQ's platform payment account.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Provider Reimbursement Obligation.</strong> If a chargeback, reversal, or payment dispute results in a financial loss to BreederHQ's platform payment account—including but not limited to the transaction amount, chargeback fees, payment processor penalties, and related costs—the Provider agrees to promptly reimburse BreederHQ for the full amount of such loss. This obligation applies regardless of the outcome of any dispute between the Provider and the Buyer.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Recovery Methods.</strong> To recover amounts owed under this section, BreederHQ may, at its sole discretion and without prior notice:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Deduct the amount from future payouts to the Provider's connected payment account;</li><li>Debit the Provider's connected payment account directly, to the extent permitted by the payment processor;</li><li>Set off the amount against any other amounts owed by BreederHQ to the Provider;</li><li>Invoice the Provider directly for the outstanding balance, payable within fifteen (15) days;</li><li>Engage collection activities or legal action for amounts that remain unpaid.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Provider Cooperation.</strong> The Provider agrees to cooperate fully with BreederHQ and the payment processor in responding to and resolving chargebacks and payment disputes, including providing transaction records, communication logs, proof of delivery, and any other evidence reasonably requested.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>No Waiver of Buyer Obligations.</strong> Nothing in this section relieves a Buyer of their obligation to pay for goods or services received. The Provider retains the right to pursue independent recovery from the Buyer for any amounts lost due to a chargeback or dispute.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">7. Disputes Between Providers and Buyers</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.1 Direct Resolution</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Providers and Buyers are expected to resolve transaction disputes directly with each other. BreederHQ encourages parties to communicate in good faith through the platform's messaging system or other channels.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.2 BreederHQ's Limited Role</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ is not an arbitrator, mediator, or adjudicator of disputes between Providers and Buyers. However, BreederHQ reserves the right to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Review reported disputes for violations of these Transaction Terms or the general Terms of Service;</li><li>Suspend or remove listings that appear fraudulent or in violation of platform policies;</li><li>Suspend or terminate accounts of users who engage in a pattern of disputes, fraud, or bad faith conduct;</li><li>Provide transaction records to either party upon request, subject to privacy considerations.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>No duty to mediate.</strong> BreederHQ has no duty to mediate, investigate, arbitrate, decide, or otherwise resolve any dispute between Users. Any help BreederHQ chooses to give, such as passing along a message, providing records it holds, or acting on a report, is voluntary, may stop at any time, does not make BreederHQ a party to the dispute, and creates no obligation to help again or to reach any particular outcome. Action BreederHQ takes to enforce its own User Agreements, such as removing a listing or suspending an account, is not a decision of a dispute between Users and does not affect their rights against each other.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.3 Fraud Reporting</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">If you believe you have been a victim of fraud on the Marketplace, you may report the incident to BreederHQ at <strong>legal@breederhq.com</strong>. BreederHQ may review fraud reports and may take action against offending accounts, at its discretion, but, subject to §4.3(c) and (d) and §10.5 of the Terms of Service, BreederHQ is not liable for losses resulting from fraudulent transactions, except to the extent caused by BreederHQ's own conduct.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.4 Credential Disputes</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ does not adjudicate the truth or authenticity of any Provider credential or Supporting Documentation. Where a Credential Dispute arises regarding a credential displayed in connection with a transaction, BreederHQ may suspend display of the credential pending the Provider's response under §8.4 of the Acceptable Use Policy. Such suspension reflects only BreederHQ's exercise of platform discretion in response to a credible report; it is not a determination by BreederHQ that the credential is invalid. Buyers and Providers retain whatever rights and remedies they have against each other directly with respect to the credential and the underlying transaction; BreederHQ is not a party to and does not adjudicate that dispute.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.5 Release for Disputes Between Users</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(a) Release.</strong> To the fullest extent permitted by law, you release BreederHQ LLC and its officers, directors, employees, agents, and affiliates from all claims, demands, damages, losses, and liabilities of every kind, known or unknown, suspected or unsuspected, arising out of or in any way connected with a dispute between you and another User, or with the acts, omissions, content, or conduct of another User, including any agreement, transaction, booking, Transaction Contract, animal, service, payment, deposit, reservation fee, refund, meeting, or communication between you and them.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(b) California Civil Code §1542.</strong> You waive the protection of California Civil Code §1542, and of any similar law of any jurisdiction, to the extent it would otherwise limit the release in paragraph (a). Section 1542 provides: "A GENERAL RELEASE DOES NOT EXTEND TO CLAIMS THAT THE CREDITOR OR RELEASING PARTY DOES NOT KNOW OR SUSPECT TO EXIST IN HIS OR HER FAVOR AT THE TIME OF EXECUTING THE RELEASE AND THAT, IF KNOWN BY HIM OR HER, WOULD HAVE MATERIALLY AFFECTED HIS OR HER SETTLEMENT WITH THE DEBTOR OR RELEASED PARTY."</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(c) What this release does not cover.</strong> This Section does not release or limit: (i) any liability of BreederHQ, or of any other person released in paragraph (a), for its own fraud, fraudulent misrepresentation, willful misconduct, or gross negligence, or for death or personal injury caused by its own negligence; (ii) BreederHQ's own obligations to you under the User Agreements, including the obligations preserved in §4.3(c) of the Terms of Service; (iii) any liability that applicable law, including California Civil Code §1668, does not permit to be released in advance; or (iv) any right or remedy that cannot lawfully be waived, including a right a Consumer has under consumer-protection law that cannot be waived. If you are a Consumer, as defined in §10.2(d) of the Terms of Service, this Section applies to you only to the extent the consumer-protection law that applies to you permits, and §10.5 of the Terms of Service applies. If you are a Consumer who lives in New Jersey, this Section does not apply to you, and whether you have released any claim against BreederHQ is determined under applicable New Jersey law. This Section does not release, limit, or affect any right or remedy you have against another User.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(d) Fallback.</strong> If any part of this Section is held unenforceable as to a particular claim or person, that part is limited to the minimum extent necessary to make it enforceable, or severed if it cannot be limited, as to that claim or person, and the rest of this Section continues in full force and effect.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(e) Same release in other User Agreements.</strong> §4.4 of the Terms of Service and §7A of the Breeder/Seller Agreement and of the Service Provider Agreement contain the same release. They are one release, stated in each document so that it reaches every User the document governs; none of them enlarges or narrows the others.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">8. Fees and Commissions</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.1 Platform Fees</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ may charge Providers a platform fee, subscription fee, or transaction commission for the use of Marketplace services. Current fee structures are published on the BreederHQ website and may be updated from time to time as provided in §8.3.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.2 Payment Processing Fees</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Payment processing fees charged by our third-party payment processor are separate from BreederHQ platform fees and are subject to the payment processor's published pricing. These fees are typically borne by the Provider unless otherwise specified.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.3 Fee Changes</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ reserves the right to modify its fee structure with at least thirty (30) days' notice to affected Providers by email to the address on file and by in-product notification. Continued use of the Marketplace after fee changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the updated fees. Where the applicable Provider Agreement sets more specific terms for a fee change, including when a price change takes effect for an existing subscription or a requirement of affirmative consent before a new recurring charge, those terms control.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">9. Prohibited Transactions</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The following transactions are prohibited on the BreederHQ Marketplace:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Sale of animals in violation of any applicable federal, state, or local law;</li><li>Sale of endangered, protected, or prohibited species without proper permits and documentation;</li><li>Sale of stolen animals or animals with disputed ownership;</li><li>Transactions involving animal fighting, cruelty, or any activity that violates animal welfare laws;</li><li>Fraudulent listings, bait-and-switch schemes, or intentional misrepresentation;</li><li>Transactions designed to circumvent tax obligations;</li><li>Sale of animals known to have contagious diseases without full disclosure;</li><li>Services the Service Provider is not legally qualified to offer under applicable law;</li><li>Any transaction that violates the BreederHQ Acceptable Use Policy.</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">10. Taxes</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">10.1 Allocation of Tax Responsibility</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">As between BreederHQ and the Provider, and except for obligations that applicable law assigns to BreederHQ, the Provider is responsible for all taxes arising from the Provider's transactions, including income, self-employment, franchise, property, and any transaction, sales, or use tax. The Provider is responsible for determining, at the time, in the manner, and in the amount required by applicable law, whether any transaction tax applies to a transaction and for collecting, reporting, and remitting it, and for obtaining and maintaining any permit, license, or registration required to do so. <strong>Nothing in this Section reallocates a nonwaivable statutory obligation of either party.</strong></p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">10.2 Provider Tax Information Warranty</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The Provider represents and warrants that all tax-related information the Provider supplies to BreederHQ or enters into the Services — including tax identification information, tax registration or permit numbers, the jurisdictions in which the Provider is registered, resale or exemption certificates, product and species classifications, and any tax rate the Provider enters — is accurate and complete when supplied, and that the Provider will promptly correct it if it becomes inaccurate. The Provider will furnish this information promptly on request.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">10.3 No Tax Advice; No Determination by BreederHQ</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Except to the extent applicable law requires BreederHQ to do so, BreederHQ does not provide tax or legal advice and does not make tax determinations for Providers. Any tax amount shown on a document relating to a Provider's transaction may be calculated using information supplied by the Provider, the Buyer, BreederHQ, the payment processor, or another source available for the transaction.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Neither the absence of a tax line on, nor a tax amount of zero shown on, any listing, invoice, receipt, or other document generated through the Services is a determination by BreederHQ that no tax applies to a transaction, and no Provider or Buyer may rely on it as such a determination.</strong></p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">10.4 Taxes BreederHQ Collects</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Where applicable law imposes on BreederHQ a nonwaivable obligation to calculate, collect, or remit a tax on a transaction, BreederHQ's obligations are governed by that law. BreederHQ may collect an amount identified as tax where BreederHQ reasonably determines that collection is required or permitted by applicable law. In either case the Provider authorizes BreederHQ to display the tax to the Buyer, add it to the amount charged, collect it at checkout, and hold and remit the amounts so collected to the relevant authority, and to request information and restrict transactions, listings, or payment methods where information necessary for that collection is not supplied.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Where BreederHQ collects a tax on a transaction under this Section, the Provider must not separately collect the same tax on that transaction, and as between the parties the Provider is relieved of collecting it.</strong> If an amount collected as tax on a transaction is determined not to be due, BreederHQ will refund it to the Buyer or remit or apply it as applicable law directs.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ may provide notice of any such program through the Services or by updating these Transaction Terms in accordance with §12. Individual advance notice of each transaction is not required.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>This Section allocates responsibilities between the parties; it does not create an independent contractual duty, enforceable by any Provider or Buyer, for BreederHQ to collect any tax beyond what applicable law requires, and no failure to collect gives rise to a claim by a Provider or Buyer except for amounts actually collected and not remitted or refunded as this Section provides.</strong></p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">10.5 Tax Reporting</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ may issue tax reporting documents (such as IRS Form 1099-K) to Providers as required by law, and will withhold where required by applicable law. Providers are responsible for providing and keeping current accurate, certified tax identification information to BreederHQ when requested. A Provider who fails to supply it may have the account suspended, may have payments withheld where applicable law requires withholding, and may be subject to backup withholding as required by law.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">10.6 Survival</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">This Section survives termination of these Transaction Terms and of the Provider's account for the period during which any relevant tax may be assessed under applicable law.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">10.7 Precedence</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">In case of any conflict among the Terms of Service, the Breeder/Seller Agreement, the Service Provider Agreement, and these Transaction Terms regarding taxes, this Section 10 controls, as provided in §13.5 of the Terms of Service.</p>
